{"name":"Tuft","hex":"#cbc2ad","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Tuft","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Tuft"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tussock grass","blocks":[{"text":"Tussock grasses are a group of grass species in the family Poaceae. They usually grow as singular plants in clumps, tufts, hummocks, or bunches, rather than forming a sod or lawn, in meadows, grasslands, and prairies. As perennial plants, most species live more than one season. Tussock grasses are often found as forage in pastures and ornamental grasses in gardens."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/East-Falkland.jpg/330px-East-Falkland.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tussock_grass"},{"title":"Fascicle (botany)","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a fascicle is a bundle of leaves or flowers growing crowded together; alternatively the term might refer to the vascular tissues that supply such an organ with nutrients. However, vascular tissues may occur in fascicles even when the organs they supply are not fascicled."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Butea_monosperma_%28Lam.%29_Taub._%28Flame_of_the_forest%29_-_Flickr_-_lalithamba.jpg/330px-Butea_monosperma_%28Lam.%29_Taub._%28Flame_of_the_forest%29_-_Flickr_-_lalithamba.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fascicle_(botany)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Konza1.jpg/500px-Konza1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Konza1.jpg/960px-Konza1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Konza1.jpg/500px-Kon